  "note": "A2 liść · THIRD pack of Oxford A2 vocab-gap batch 2 (VOCAB-BUILD-DIGEST batch 2). Grouping rationale: twelve Oxford-A2 nouns from school and study — matematyka, fizyka, chemia, biologia, architektura, ankieta, odkrycie, wynalazek, rysunek, esej, wstęp, pamiętnik. Thirteen gap rows, because Oxford lists mathematics and maths separately and both are matematyka. leaf_school_a1 and a2_school2 already own szkoła, uczeń, student, klasa, lekcja, wykład, uniwersytet, egzamin, sprawdzian, zadanie, zdanie, ocena, błąd, praca domowa, ćwiczenie, zeszyt, tablica, ołówek, długopis, historia, geografia, nauki ścisłe, język polski, przedmiot, książka, czytanie, pisanie, powtarzać, zdać, oblać — ANCHORS, never re-taught. The pack rides miec_acc plus the -uje and -isz present tenses, so teaches_structures is [] by construction. Judgment calls, all reported: (1) THE NODE ID IS a2_subjects, NOT a2_school2. a2_school2 is a LIVE pack at path index 80 („W szkole\" / Learning & school) and this one was drafted under that id before the collision was caught; the id was checked against tree.json and freed rather than assumed. Recording it because the gap build will keep wanting obvious ids that A1/A2 already hold. (2) THIS PACK IS BUILT ON VERBS BECAUSE THE ADJECTIVES DO NOT EXIST. The natural things to say about a school subject are that it is hard, easy, important or interesting, and the pool has NONE of trudny, łatwy, ważny or interesujący in any gender, while ciekawy exists only in the masculine — which is no use to six feminine nouns. Rather than bend the grammar or invent an adjective, the pack says what you DO with a subject: Studiuję fizykę, Lubię biologię, Moja siostra lubi chemię. That is also the more useful Polish. (3) THE SECOND BLOCK IS AN ACCUSATIVE BOARD AND SO WAS a2_food3's, one batch earlier. The repeat is deliberate and is named here rather than hidden: the accusative is what these nouns need, -a → -ę is the single most productive ending an A2 learner meets, and inventing a different second block to avoid looking repetitive would have cost the pack its point. The board carries the -ia → -ię pair (chemia → chemię, biologia → biologię) that food3 had no example of, and closes with Lubię rysunek to show a masculine that does not move. (4) wiedza ('knowledge') WAS DRAFTED AND CUT. It is abstract, and with no taught word for hard, easy, important or useful there was nothing true to say about it at this level. Its row stays in the gap file for a pack that can carry it; nothing was authored and nothing deleted. pamiętnik took its slot — concrete, a real Oxford A2 row ('diary'), and easy to talk about. (5) ankieta is glossed 'survey (a set of questions)' because an English speaker reading 'survey' may reach for a land survey or a general look-round; the Polish word is only the questionnaire sense. (6) wstęp is glossed as the first part of a book or a talk, and its explain also names the 'entry' sense, because a learner who meets Wstęp wolny on a door should not read it as 'free introduction'. (7) NO ICONS. Every candidate emoji for these words is either a school building (reads as szkoła, taught) or a book (reads as książka, taught); the same rule that emptied the icon set in a2_people3 empties it here. (8) TWO EXPLAINS WERE REWRITTEN AFTER A POOL CHECK: the first drafts cited odkryć and pamiętać as roots, and neither verb is taught anywhere — an explain may not introduce Polish the learner has not met, even in passing.",
